  "justification": "This order ranks all 169 starting-hand classes from strongest to weakest by one objective measure: the share of the pot each hand wins when it is all in before the flop against three opponents, each holding any random two cards. Each number was computed with this project's own equity calculator, using the class's lowest-numbered combo and every unseen combo as each opponent's range, with 30,000 sampled deals seeded from the input, then rounded to one decimal place. Hands with equal rounded numbers keep the starting-hand grid order. Against three hands, suited connectors such as 76s rank above offsuit hands with one high card such as Q2o, which is closer to how they play at a real table. The order is used only when an observed opponent's preflop range is resized to match how often that player raises or calls: a wider range adds the strongest hands from this list that the typical-player range lacks, and a narrower range keeps the strongest of the typical-player hands, always at least one.",
